														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2853657">
									

<p>3.5&#160;km is a nigh impossible depth for someone using only scuba gear. At depths much lower than that, the pressure can cause the air the person is breathing to become toxic. Nitrogen can induce an intoxicated state at just 30 meters. Oxygen can become acutely toxicity at 60 meters. Even inert helium, used by divers to dilute their air mixtures, can cause convulsions at 150 meters. The deepest anyone has dived using scuba gear is 332 meters.</p>

